INT. FENCING SALLE - EVENING

Wooden floor, mirrored wall. Masks hang on pegs. Two figures in white square off under a single hanging lamp.

LORENZO "ENZO" BIANCHI, 20s, wiry, tightens his glove. Opposite, PRIYANKA SHARMA-ODUYA, 20s, calm, flexes her blade.

ENZO
Priya, you're stalling.

PRIYA
I'm warming up.

ENZO
It's your finals bout.

PRIYA
It's practice.

They salute. En garde. Silence. The lamp hums.

Lunge. Parry. The blades sing. They circle, step, retreat, advance, a quiet dance.

ENZO
Bit slow tonight.

PRIYA
Bit loud tonight.

Click. Point to Priya. She grins. He grins back.

The door opens. A tall, silver-haired man in a long coat steps in. MASTER ALBERIC DUVAL, 70s, leans on a cane and watches.

ALBERIC
Don't stop on my account.

ENZO
Maestro.

PRIYA
Master Duval.

ALBERIC
Again.

They resume. Faster now. Blades blur. A final parry. A riposte. Priya stops, blade at Enzo's chest.

PRIYA
Touch.

Alberic nods, slowly, and turns to go. At the door, he pauses.

ALBERIC
Priyanka. Pack your bag. Nationals are Thursday.
